                     </origin>
                     <provenance source="5271"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_514">Southwick,
                           Hampshire. Augustinian priory of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>London,
                           BL MSS Cotton Otho B.xi, Add. 34652 (fol. 2), and Cotton Otho B.x (fols.
                           55, 58, and 62) were originally one volume.</p><p>A Southwick inscription
                           stretched across pp. 18–19 of the unburnt MS (see Wanley in Bodleian,
                           Gough London 54).</p><p>Part of another inscription occurs at the foot of
                           fol. 28: 'fecerit quo minus eiusdem Ecclesie sit seu qui hunc titulum
                           dolo [...] deleuerit. nisi condigne eidem [...] Amen. Amen' (s.
                           xiii).</p><p>Seen by Th. Rudborne at Southwick in s. xv (see Wharton,
                           Anglia Sacra, i, 183).</p><p>Seen by Leland at Southwick (CBMLC
                           A31.3).</p><p>The Bede is in the same script as the Parker Chronicle
                           (CCCC 173) for the years 924–55, which was at Winchester. The Chronicle
                           is a copy of the Parker Chronicle to the year 1001.</p><p>Now much
                           burnt.</p><p>BL MS Add. 43703 is a copy of s. xvi (except of the leaf in
                           Add.). Add. 34652 belonged to Tanner and Th. Astle.</p><p>See Ker, Cat.
                           of MSS containing Anglo-Saxon, 230–234.</p></provenance>
                     <provenance cert="low" source="5740"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_437"
                           >Winchester, Hampshire. Benedictine cathedral priory of St Peter, St
                           Paul, and St Swithun</orgName><p>A detached leaf of Cotton Otho
                        B.xi.</p></provenance>
                  </history>
